      transliteration: 'idaṁ śreṣṭhaṁ jyotiṣāṁ jyotirāgāccitraḥ praketo ajaniṣṭa vibhvā\nyathā prasūtā savituḥ savāyam̐ evā rātryuṣase yonimāraik',
      translation: 'This light has come, the fairest of all lights; the bright, far-reaching radiance is born. As Night was set in motion at Savitar\'s command, so she has yielded up her place to Dawn.',
